Title: THE LEDGER
Credit: Written by
Author: A. Sample
Draft date: First draft

FADE IN:

INT. HALVORSEN & PRICE LLP - CONFERENCE ROOM - NIGHT

Forty floors above Boston Harbor. Rain streaks the glass. A long table littered with banker's boxes.

DANIEL REYES (38), junior partner, sleeves rolled, stares at a spreadsheet on a Dell laptop. A cold cup of Dunkin' coffee beside him.

Across the table, MARGARET HALVORSEN (61), founding partner, pearls, reading glasses on a chain, closes a folder.

MARGARET
The Whitcombe account closes Friday. Nobody looks at the 2019 transfers again.

DANIEL
Three million moved through a shell in Delaware. Someone signed off on that.

MARGARET
Someone did. And that someone bills two thousand an hour.

She leaves. Daniel keeps scrolling. He stops. Zooms in. A wire to "NORTHSTAR CONSULTING GROUP."

INT. DANIEL'S APARTMENT - SOUTH END - LATER

A one-bedroom on Tremont Street. Boxes still unpacked. A Sonos speaker plays "Blue in Green." Daniel pours a Sam Adams and opens a MacBook.

He types NORTHSTAR CONSULTING into a search bar. An address: 114 STATE STREET, SUITE 900.

His phone buzzes. Caller ID: LENA.

INT. THE BANSHEE PUB - DORCHESTER - NIGHT

A neighborhood bar, Bruins game on a Samsung TV over the taps. LENA OKAFOR (35), investigative reporter for the BOSTON HERALD, nurses a Guinness.

Daniel slides in across from her.

LENA
You said you had something.

DANIEL
I said I might.

LENA
That's a lawyer's might.

DANIEL
Northstar Consulting Group. Ever heard of it?

LENA
No. Should I have?

DANIEL
It's registered to a mailbox on State Street. It received three million dollars from a client of mine and it doesn't consult anyone.

LENA
Who's the client?

Daniel says nothing. Lena laughs.

LENA (CONT'D)
You want me to find it without you saying it. Fine. I'm good at that.

EXT. STATE STREET - DAY

Daniel walks past 114 State Street. A UPS Store. Mailboxes inside. He photographs the sign with his iPhone.

A black Cadillac Escalade idles across the street. Behind the wheel, VICTOR BRANDT (50s), ex-Boston PD, now "security consultant." He watches Daniel go.

INT. HALVORSEN & PRICE LLP - DANIEL'S OFFICE - DAY

A knock. PATRICK WHITCOMBE (48), CEO of WHITCOMBE MARITIME, a tan that didn't happen in Massachusetts, steps in uninvited.

PATRICK
Margaret says you've been thorough.

DANIEL
It's what you pay for.

PATRICK
I pay for outcomes, Daniel. Thoroughness is how associates get promoted. Outcomes are how partners stay partners.

He puts a business card on the desk. It reads WHITCOMBE MARITIME, 1 HARBOR TOWER, BOSTON. Phone 617-555-0142.

PATRICK (CONT'D)
Call me if you find anything that worries you. Me. Not her.

INT. LENA'S CAR - NIGHT

A dented Toyota Camry outside the SUFFOLK COUNTY REGISTRY OF DEEDS. Lena flips through printouts by the dome light. A name is circled: ANTHONY DESALVO, listed as registered agent for Northstar.

She dials. Speakerphone.

LENA
Mr. DeSalvo? Lena Okafor, Boston Herald. I'm calling about a company you're the registered agent for --

CLICK. Dial tone.

INT. THE BANSHEE PUB - NIGHT

Daniel and Lena, same booth. Between them, the printout.

LENA
Anthony DeSalvo. Sixty-two. Retired from the Massachusetts State Police in 2011. Now he's the registered agent for eleven companies and every one of them is a PO box.

DANIEL
So he's a name for hire.

LENA
He's a name for hire who used to run the financial crimes unit. That's not an accident. That's a resume.

DANIEL
Whitcombe Maritime is a shipping company. Why does a shipping company need a shell that launders --

He stops himself. Lena raises an eyebrow.

LENA
You said the word.

DANIEL
I didn't say it. I stopped before it.

LENA
You're a terrible lawyer.

INT. HALVORSEN & PRICE LLP - MARGARET'S OFFICE - DAY

Floor-to-ceiling. A Rothko print. Margaret pours two Macallan 18s at eleven in the morning.

MARGARET
Patrick tells me you've been photographing his mail.

DANIEL
I photographed a UPS Store.

MARGARET
Daniel. I have been at this firm since before you were born. There is a version of this conversation where you make partner in two years. There is another version.

She slides a document across the desk. A partnership agreement. His name is already typed in.

MARGARET (CONT'D)
Sign it, and the Whitcombe file goes to storage. Closed. Forever.

Daniel stares at it.

EXT. HARBOR TOWER - LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

Daniel, in a hoodie, meets Lena behind a dumpster. Lena hands him a FedEx envelope.

LENA
Wire records. DeSalvo's shells to an account at FIRST MERIDIAN BANK in the Caymans. Same account paid Victor Brandt's security firm forty grand last March.

DANIEL
The guy in the Escalade.

LENA
The guy in the Escalade who used to be Patrick Whitcombe's driver. Before he was a cop. Before he was fired for being a cop who was also a driver.

Headlights. The Escalade. Brandt gets out, casual, hands in his jacket.

BRANDT
Counselor. Ms. Okafor. Beautiful night.

LENA
Victor.

BRANDT
You've got a nice little scene going here. Behind a dumpster. Like a movie.

DANIEL
Is there something you want?

BRANDT
Patrick wants you to know that he read your bar admission file. Nice write-up on that DUI in 2014. Would be a shame if the Board of Bar Overseers had to look at it again.

He smiles. Gets back in the car. Drives off.

LENA
He knows about your DUI?

DANIEL
It was a plea. There's no conviction.

LENA
There's a file.

INT. DANIEL'S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Daniel at the kitchen counter, MacBook open, Sonos silent now. He pulls up the partnership agreement PDF. He pulls up Lena's wire records.

He opens Gmail. Recipient: tips@bostonherald.com. Subject line: Whitcombe / Northstar / Halvorsen.

His finger hovers.

Phone buzzes. Text from MARGARET: "Friday. 9 AM. Bring a pen."

He closes the email draft. Opens a new one.

Recipient: Assistant U.S. Attorney CAROLINE MERCER, District of Massachusetts.

INT. JOHN JOSEPH MOAKLEY U.S. COURTHOUSE - CONFERENCE ROOM - DAY

Federal beige. CAROLINE MERCER (44), AUSA, sits with two FBI agents. Daniel across from them with a single banker's box.

MERCER
You understand you're waiving privilege on everything in that box.

DANIEL
I understand the firm is going to argue it was never mine to waive.

MERCER
And you're doing it anyway.

DANIEL
I've read the partnership agreement. Page nine has a clause about "reputational matters." It was written for me.

Mercer opens the box. On top: the Northstar wire. Under it: the Halvorsen signature.

MERCER
Mr. Reyes. You are going to be a very unpopular man on State Street.

DANIEL
I live on Tremont.

FADE OUT.

THE END
